Build and run flex 2.6.4 on Windows (MSVC).

Upstream flex has no Windows port: as of master (4fcc714, 2026-07) src/filter.c
still runs the output pipeline as forked child processes, and configure.ac's
AC_FUNC_FORK has no fallback behind it.  This patch adds the support the registry
module needs, keeping the generated scanners byte for byte what the POSIX build
produces.

src/filter.c
  The output pipeline without fork().  Upstream feeds the generated scanner text
  through a chain of children: the tee filter copies it to a second m4 for the
  --header-file, m4 expands the skeleton macros, and a last filter renumbers the
  #line directives.  Here the text is kept in a temporary file while flex runs;
  filter_finish() then spawns m4 (_spawnvp, _P_WAIT) over it once for the scanner
  and once more for the header, with the same preamble and footer the tee writes,
  and runs the #line fix-up in this process.  The preamble/footer writers and the
  fix-up loop are factored out of filter_tee_header / filter_fix_linedirs so both
  paths share them; the POSIX path is otherwise unchanged.  The one difference from
  upstream: with -t (scanner to stdout) the #line directives are not renumbered,
  since a terminal cannot be rewritten; rules_flex always passes -o.  Temporary
  files are created with _O_CREAT|_O_EXCL|_O_TEMPORARY on names from _tempnam,
  retrying while the name exists: tmpfile() wants the drive's root directory,
  and _tempnam's names repeat across processes, so concurrent flex actions
  sharing %TEMP% would otherwise truncate each other's files.
  The regex-based blank-line test becomes is_blank_line(): MSVC has no <regex.h>
  for that pattern (see src/regex.c).

src/main.c
  flex_main calls filter_finish() before the output file is closed; the earlier
  Windows preamble written from main is gone (each m4 pass writes its own).  The
  $PATH walk for m4 splits on ';'.  program_name is argv[0] as given and
  --version prints "flex"/"flex++" rather than the executable's name.

src/flexdef.h, src/regex.c, src/scanopt.c
  Declarations for the above; <regex.h>-free implementations of the two regexes
  flex compiles; MSVC-compatible option scanning.

Regenerate with: apply hardcode_int_max_log10.patch to a pristine flex-2.6.4
as flex-2.6.4-orig, edit the five files in a copy flex-2.6.4-mod, then
`diff -ruN flex-2.6.4-orig flex-2.6.4-mod` over those files.  Keep the
`diff -ruN` lines: Bazel's patch applier needs them to tell the files apart.

